From: Claude (Cowork mode)
Date: 2026-05-10
Subject: [PATCH] docs: scrub bootstrap password from DEPLOYMENT.md

⚠ DO NOT APPLY THIS PATCH UNTIL the operator has completed
secret_rotation_runbook.md §3 (rotated every real user password
in production). Applying earlier only obfuscates without protecting:
the password is already in git history on origin/main, and a casual
diff observer can recover it.

After §3 is done, apply with:

    cd C:\Users\Administrator\Desktop\convera-platform
    git apply docs/patches/DEPLOYMENT_md_scrub.patch
    git diff DEPLOYMENT.md       # review
    git add DEPLOYMENT.md
    git commit -m "docs: scrub rotated bootstrap password from DEPLOYMENT.md"

Patch removes 7 occurrences of the literal `<old bootstrap password redacted>` and replaces
them with `<rotated — see docs/secret_rotation_runbook.md §3>`. It
also adds a "WARNING — historical leak" note at the top of the User
Accounts section so readers understand that git history retains the
old value.

